+# Security policy
+
+## SSH host-key verification
+
+OhMyPanel verifies the SSH server host key before sending a password or using a private key.
+
+- A previously trusted key must match the entry in the app-owned `known_hosts` file.
+- A server seen for the first time is blocked until the user explicitly confirms the displayed SHA-256 fingerprint.
+- The confirmation retry is bound to that exact fingerprint. A different key presented between the prompt and retry is rejected.
+- A changed key is always rejected and is never overwritten automatically, including during automatic reconnect.
+
+The `known_hosts` path is shown in host-key error messages. On Unix systems the app applies mode `0600` to this file.
+
+After a legitimate server rebuild or host-key rotation, verify the new fingerprint through the provider console or another trusted channel. Then remove only the obsolete entry from the displayed `known_hosts` file and reconnect. Do not delete or replace an entry merely to suppress a warning.
+
+## Reporting vulnerabilities
+
+Open a private GitHub security advisory for this repository when possible. Avoid including credentials, private keys, server addresses, or other sensitive deployment data in public issues.
